## Original Content
Turbopuffer cofounder Simon Eskildsen on the benefits of longer tenure, using first principles to build durable software &#8211; and why founders should be cautious when raising VC money

## Summary
The article features Simon Eskildsen, cofounder of Turbopuffer, discussing the advantages of longer employee tenure in companies. He emphasizes using first principles to create durable software and warns founders about the risks of raising venture capital money.

## Key Points
- Benefits of longer tenure in companies for software development and knowledge retention.
- Application of first principles in software engineering to build durable and efficient systems.
- Caution advised for startup founders when seeking venture capital funding to maintain control.
- The use of 'napkin math' as a practical method to push the limits of software engineering efficiency.


